.TH TOFF 1 "August 2026" "toff 1.0.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
toff \- shutdown timer with YouTube/media URL support

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B toff
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI<TIME|URL>\fR
.br
.B toff
\fB\-\-cancel\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B toff
schedules a safe system poweroff after a specified duration.
Time can be given directly or extracted automatically from a YouTube video,
playlist, or any media URL supported by \fByt-dlp\fR(1).

.SH TIME FORMATS
.TP
.B H.MM
Hours and minutes (e.g.\& \fB1.30\fR = 1 hour 30 minutes).
.TP
.B MM
Minutes only (e.g.\& \fB90\fR = 90 minutes).
.TP
.B HH:MM
Hours and minutes (e.g.\& \fB1:30\fR).
.TP
.B HH:MM:SS
Full duration (e.g.\& \fB1:30:00\fR).

.SH URL SUPPORT
When a URL is given, \fBtoff\fR uses \fByt-dlp\fR to fetch the media duration.
YouTube playlists are auto-detected and all video durations are summed.
Over 1000 sites are supported including SoundCloud and Vimeo.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-buffer " " \fIMINUTES\fR
Add extra buffer time after the media ends. Default is 2 minutes.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-playlist
Force playlist mode: fetch and sum all durations in the playlist.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-playlist
Disable automatic playlist detection.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-banner
Skip the ASCII art banner animation.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the live countdown display.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cancel
Cancel a pending \fBtoff\fR shutdown.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
Shut down in 1 hour and 30 minutes:
.RS
.B toff 1.30
.RE

Shut down in 90 minutes:
.RS
.B toff 90
.RE

Shut down after a YouTube video ends (+ 2 min buffer):
.RS
.B toff https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ
.RE

Shut down after a playlist with a 5-minute buffer:
.RS
.B toff \-\-buffer 5 \-\-playlist 'https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PL...'
.RE

Cancel a pending shutdown:
.RS
.B toff \-\-cancel
.RE

.SH SHUTDOWN STRATEGY
.B toff
tries multiple scheduling strategies in order:
.IP 1. 4
\fBshutdown\fR command (survives terminal close; most portable)
.IP 2. 4
\fBsystemd-run --on-active\fR (precise timer, systemd only)
.IP 3. 4
\fBat\fR command (cross-distro, survives terminal close)
.IP 4. 4
Background \fBsleep\fR + \fBpoweroff\fR (universal fallback)

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR}/toff/
Runtime state directory. Stores timer PID, scheduling method, and keepalive PID.
Removed automatically on cancel.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B yt-dlp
Required for URL mode. Install with \fBsudo pacman \-S yt\-dlp\fR on Arch Linux.
.TP
.B bash >= 4.0
Required for associative arrays and other features.
.TP
.B getopt
Required for argument parsing (part of util-linux).

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid input, missing dependency, scheduling failure).

